# Panel saveInPreset Storage Pattern

**Source:** [Forum Topic](https://forum.hise.audio/topic/12635)

**Tags:** Scripting, trusted

Dynamically created panels with Content.addPanel used as invisible preset storage containers. Uses a delayed setTimerCallback to set saveInPreset after the panel value is initialized, working around the timing requirement that data must be stored before enabling preset saving. Demonstrates the difference between storing undefined vs defined values.

```javascript
Content.makeFrontInterface(600, 600);

inline function addStoragePanel(id, data)
{
	if (Content.componentExists(id))
		return Content.getComponent(id);

	local comp = Content.addPanel(id, 0, 0);
	comp.setValue(data);
	comp.set("visible", false);

	//	set "saveToPreset" delayed otherwise the
	//	object to save will not be stored in the panel
	comp.setTimerCallback(function()
	{
		this.set("saveInPreset", true);
		this.stopTimer();
	});

	comp.startTimer(1000);

	return comp;
}

//	========= set objects to save for the panels ===============

//	P1 is set to save an object with a undefined value and an empty array
//	this panel will lose the applied value after one compile and log value 0.0
const P1 = addStoragePanel("P1", {"state": undefined, "data": []});

//	P2 is set to save an object with a defined value and an array with content
//	this will be stored in the panel as it should
const P2 = addStoragePanel("P2", {"state": false, "data": ["some string", 7, 12.03]});


inline function onP1Control(component, value)
{
	Console.print(trace(component.getValue()));
}

P1.setControlCallback(onP1Control);


inline function onP2Control(component, value)
{
	Console.print(trace(component.getValue()));
}

P2.setControlCallback(onP2Control);


inline function onTestControl(component, value)
{
	if (value)
	{
		Console.print(trace(P1.getValue()));
		Console.print(trace(P2.getValue()));
	}
};

Content.getComponent("Test").setControlCallback(onTestControl);
```

