# Table Snap Values Generator

**Source:** [Forum Topic](https://forum.hise.audio/topic/7375)

**Tags:** General Questions, trusted

Utility function that generates evenly-spaced snap values for a ScriptTable using setSnapValues. Divides the 0-1 range into equal segments based on the desired number of snaps.

```javascript
Content.makeFrontInterface(600, 600);

const var Table = Content.getComponent("Table");

inline function setTableSnapValues(table, snaps)
{
	local values = [];
	local snap = 1 / snaps;

	for (i = 0; i < snaps; i++)
		values.push(snap * i);

	values.push(1.0);
	table.setSnapValues(values);
}

setTableSnapValues(Table, 20);
```

# Table Snap Values with Visual Grid

**Source:** [Forum Topic](https://forum.hise.audio/topic/7375)

**Tags:** General Questions, trusted

Table snap values with a panel overlay drawing vertical grid lines at each snap position. Uses a panel setValue to pass the snap array, then draws grid lines proportionally spaced across the panel width in setPaintRoutine.

```javascript
Content.makeFrontInterface(600, 600);

const var Table = Content.getComponent("Table");
const var TableGrid = Content.getComponent("TableGrid");

//	SET SNAP VALUE
inline function setTableSnapValues(table, snaps)
{
	local values = [];
	local snap = 1 / snaps;

	for (i = 0; i < snaps; i++)
		values.push(snap * i);

	values.push(1.0);

	table.setSnapValues(values);
	TableGrid.setValue(values);
	TableGrid.changed();
}

//	EXECUTE
setTableSnapValues(Table, 20);


//	WITH GRID
TableGrid.setPaintRoutine(function(g)
{
	g.setColour(Colours.chartreuse);

	if (typeof this.getValue() == "object")
	{
		var space = this.getWidth() / (this.getValue().length - 1);

		for (i = 0; i <= this.getValue().length; i++)
			g.drawLine(i * space, i * space, 4, this.getHeight() - 4, 0.2);
	}

});
```

# Table with Grid Factory Function

**Source:** [Forum Topic](https://forum.hise.audio/topic/7375)

**Tags:** General Questions, trusted

Factory function using Content.addPanel and Content.addTable with parentComponent to create a self-contained table-with-grid widget. Dynamically creates container, grid overlay, and table components with setSnapValues and a paint routine for visual grid lines.

```javascript
Content.makeFrontInterface(600, 600);

//	TABLE W GRID FACTORY (name, x, y, width, height, number of snaps)
inline function createTableWithGrid(name, x, y, w, h, numsnaps)
{
	local container = Content.addPanel(name + "Container", x, y);
	Content.setPropertiesFromJSON(name + "Container",
	{
"type": "ScriptPanel",
"id": name + "Container",
"x": x,
"y": y,
"width": w,
"height": h,
		"bgColour": 16777215,
		"itemColour": 0,
		"itemColour2": 0,
		"textColour": 16777215,
	});

	local grid = Content.addPanel(name + "Grid");
	Content.setPropertiesFromJSON(name + "Grid",
	{
"type": "ScriptPanel",
"id": name + "Grid",
		"x": 0,
		"y": 0,
"width": w,
"height": h,
"parentComponent": name + "Container"
	});

	local table = Content.addTable(name);
	Content.setPropertiesFromJSON(name,
	{
"type": "ScriptTable",
"id": name,
		"x": 0,
		"y": 0,
"width": w,
"height": h,
"saveInPreset": true,
"parentComponent": name + "Container"
	});

	local values = [];
	local snap = 1 / numsnaps;

	for (i = 0; i < numsnaps; i++)
		values.push(snap * i);

	values.push(1.0);

	table.setSnapValues(values);
	grid.setValue(values);
	grid.changed();

	grid.setPaintRoutine(function(g)
	{
		g.setColour(Colours.chartreuse);

		if (typeof this.getValue() == "object")
		{
			var space = this.getWidth() / (this.getValue().length - 1);

			for (j = 0; j <= this.getValue().length; j++)
				g.drawLine(j * space, j * space, 4, this.getHeight() - 4, 0.2);
		}
	});
}

//	CREATE	------------
const Tbl = createTableWithGrid("Tbl", 100, 100, 400, 200, 20);
```

# Path Follow Animation with getPointOnPath

**Source:** [Forum Topic](https://forum.hise.audio/topic/7373)

**Tags:** General Questions, trusted

Content.createPath with quadraticTo to define a curved path, then getPointOnPath with getLength to position a panel along the path driven by a knob. Draws the path on a background panel and moves a foreground panel using setPosition.

```javascript
Content.makeFrontInterface(600, 600);

const var pathPnl = Content.getComponent("pathPnl");
const var Panel1 = Content.getComponent("Panel1");


const var p = Content.createPath();
p.startNewSubPath(50, 250);
p.quadraticTo(350, 100, 200, 50);
p.quadraticTo(50, 100, 350, 250);


pathPnl.setPaintRoutine(function(g)
{
	g.setColour(0xffff0000);

	if (true)
		g.drawPath(p, p.getBounds(1.0), 1.0);
});


inline function onKnob1Control(component, value)
{
	local point = p.getPointOnPath(p.getLength() * value);
	local posX = point[0] + pathPnl.get("x") - Panel1.getWidth() / 2.0;
	local posY = point[1] + pathPnl.get("y") - Panel1.getHeight() / 2.0;

	Panel1.setPosition(posX, posY, Panel1.getWidth(), Panel1.getHeight());
};

Content.getComponent("Knob1").setControlCallback(onKnob1Control);
```

# Ring Shape Mouse Hit Detection

**Source:** [Forum Topic](https://forum.hise.audio/topic/7373)

**Tags:** General Questions, trusted

Panel setMouseCallback with Math.sqrt distance calculation to detect whether the mouse is within a donut/ring shape. Computes distance from center and checks against inner and outer radii for visual feedback.

```javascript
Content.makeFrontInterface(600, 600);
Console.clear();

const var Panel1 = Content.getComponent("Panel1");

const var outer = 250;
const var inner = 200;

Panel1.setPaintRoutine(function(g)
{
	g.fillAll(Colours.black);

	g.setColour(this.data.isValid ? Colours.green : Colours.darkred);
	g.fillEllipse([(this.getWidth() - outer) / 2.0, (this.getHeight() - outer) / 2.0, outer, outer]);
	g.setColour(Colours.black);
	g.fillEllipse([(this.getWidth() - inner) / 2.0, (this.getHeight() - inner) / 2.0, inner, inner]);
});


Panel1.setMouseCallback(function(event)
{
	var posX = event.x - this.getWidth() / 2.0;
	var posY = event.y - this.getHeight() / 2.0;

	var l = Math.sqrt((posX * posX) + (posY * posY));

	this.data.isValid = l < outer / 2.0 && l > inner / 2.0;
	this.repaint();
});
```

